_Last updated: 26 August 2026. Rewritten against current 2026 data from BrightLocal, Backlinko, Shopify, Whitespark, and Ahrefs, with sources linked throughout instead of only named._

## Local SEO Statistics 2026 (Quick Answer)

The numbers that actually move local SEO decisions in 2026:

- Local Pack position 1 gets a **17.8%** click share, position 2 **13.6%**, position 3 **10.4%**, adding up to roughly **42%** of all clicks on a local results page (BrightLocal, Backlinko, 2026)
- A complete Google Business Profile earns **7x more clicks** than an incomplete one. The average profile gets around **1,260 views**, **428 website clicks**, and **340 direction requests** a month (Google, BrightLocal, 2026)
- **76%** of "near me" mobile searches lead to a business visit within 24 hours, and **78%** of local mobile searches convert to an offline purchase (Backlinko, 2026)
- Businesses with **50 or more reviews** are **266% more likely** to appear in the Local Pack, though the businesses that actually hold a top-three spot average **561 reviews** each (BrightLocal, Shopify, 2026)
- Replying to reviews shows no proven direct effect on rankings. It functions as a trust factor instead: **88%** of consumers say they'd use a business that replies to all its reviews, against **47%** for one that never responds (BrightLocal, 2026)
- AI Overviews now appear on a large share of local business searches and have cut click-through to the top organic result by **34.5% to 58%**, depending on which 2026 dataset you look at (Ahrefs, 2026)

